  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Distributed Transactions and Two-Phase Commit",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Distributed Transactions and Two-Phase Commit",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Problem",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "One logical operation spans several ==databases or services==",
                "It must commit ==everywhere or nowhere== (atomic commit)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Two Phases",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Prepare",
                    "sub": "coordinator asks all",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Vote",
                    "sub": "log, then YES or NO",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Decide",
                    "sub": "COMMIT or ABORT",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Ack",
                    "sub": "participants confirm",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:Phase 1}: participant durably logs its vote; a ==YES is a promise== it can still commit",
                "{green:Phase 2}: all YES gives ==COMMIT==; any NO or timeout gives ==ABORT==",
                "Coordinator ==logs the decision before sending== it"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Blocking and Alternatives",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Coordinator crashes after YES votes: participants keep ==locks==, stuck ==in-doubt==, cannot decide alone until it recovers"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "2PC",
                "3PC",
                "2PC + Paxos/Raft"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Phases",
                  "prepare, decide",
                  "adds pre-commit",
                  "same as 2PC"
                ],
                [
                  "Coordinator crash",
                  "blocks",
                  "less blocking",
                  "replicated, survives"
                ],
                [
                  "Partition",
                  "blocks",
                  "still breaks",
                  "safe"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Real systems",
              "text": "Do not rely on 3PC. Make the coordinator fault-tolerant with ==Paxos or Raft==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Sagas and the Transactional Outbox",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Sagas and the Transactional Outbox",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a Saga Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Saga== = sequence of **local transactions**, no global lock",
                "Each step has a ==compensating action== that undoes it semantically",
                "Examples: refund payment, cancel reservation"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Orchestration vs Choreography",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Orchestration",
                "Choreography"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Control",
                  "Central orchestrator tells each service the next step and tracks state",
                  "Services react to each other's events, no controller"
                ],
                [
                  "Good",
                  "Easy to follow and debug",
                  "{green:Loosely coupled}"
                ],
                [
                  "Risk",
                  "{red:Central coupling point}",
                  "Flow hard to trace, cyclic dependencies creep in"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Saga Caveats",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "No ==isolation==: others can see intermediate state",
                "Use ==semantic locks== or **pending** states",
                "Steps and compensations must be ==idempotent== and retryable"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Transactional Outbox",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "One local tx",
                    "sub": "business row + outbox row",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Relay",
                    "sub": "poller or CDC (Debezium)",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Broker",
                    "sub": "publish",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Fixes dual write",
              "text": "DB commit and broker publish can no longer diverge. Delivery is ==at-least-once==, so consumers must be **idempotent**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Exactly-Once Myths and Idempotency",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Exactly-Once Myths and Idempotency",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Delivery Guarantees",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Guarantee",
                "Failure",
                "How"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "At-most-once",
                  "may ==lose==",
                  "send, never retry"
                ],
                [
                  "At-least-once",
                  "may ==duplicate==",
                  "retry until ack"
                ],
                [
                  "Exactly-once delivery",
                  "{red:impossible}",
                  "Two Generals"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Lost message and lost ack look the same to the sender",
                "Goal: ==exactly-once processing== (effectively-once)",
                "= at-least-once delivery + {green:idempotent consumer}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Idempotency Key and Dedup",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Client",
                    "sub": "unique request ID",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Server",
                    "sub": "look up the ID",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Seen",
                    "sub": "return stored result",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "New",
                    "sub": "run, store ID + result",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Record message ID in the ==same DB transaction== as the side effect",
                "Or a ==unique constraint== or upsert: a replay is a no-op"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "BEGIN;",
                "INSERT INTO processed(msg_id) VALUES ('m-42');",
                "UPDATE accounts SET bal = bal - 10 WHERE id = 1;",
                "COMMIT;"
              ],
              "note": "duplicate msg_id breaks the primary key, so everything rolls back"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Kafka Limits",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Kafka 'exactly-once'",
              "items": [
                "Idempotent producer + transactions",
                "Holds only inside Kafka read-process-write",
                "Emails and HTTP calls sit **outside** Kafka",
                "They still need idempotency"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Exactly-once delivery is a myth. Build ==effectively-once== with retries plus dedup."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Leader Election and Raft Basics",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Leader Election and Raft Basics",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Leader Election",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "One node is the ==leader== and coordinates writes",
                "Safety: ==at most one leader per term== (epoch)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Raft Roles and Quorum",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Follower",
                    "sub": "no heartbeat in time",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Candidate",
                    "sub": "term+1, requests votes",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Leader",
                    "sub": "wins majority",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Time is split into ==numbered terms==",
                "Election timeout is ==randomized== so ties are rare",
                "One vote per node per term; win needs `N/2+1`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Nodes",
                "Quorum",
                "Tolerates"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "3",
                  "2",
                  "1 failure"
                ],
                [
                  "5",
                  "3",
                  "2 failures"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Use ==odd== sizes: an extra even node adds no tolerance"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Replication and Split Brain",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Leader appends the write, sends `AppendEntries`",
                "Commit once a ==majority== has stored the entry",
                "Candidate with a less up-to-date log cannot win",
                "Partitioned old leader cannot commit: no majority",
                "It sees a ==higher term== and steps down"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "The term number is the fence: a higher term always beats a stale leader."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Distributed Locks, Fencing Tokens, ZooKeeper and etcd",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Distributed Locks, Fencing Tokens, ZooKeeper and etcd",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Leases and Why They Break",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Lease== lock: expires after a **TTL**, so a crashed holder can't block forever"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "SET lock:job42 clientA NX PX 30000"
              ],
              "note": "NX = only if absent, PX = TTL in ms"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "GC pause or slow network: lease expires, client still thinks it holds it",
                "Result: {red:two holders} write at once"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Fencing Tokens",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "A gets token 33",
                    "sub": "then GC pause",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "B gets token 34",
                    "sub": "writes OK",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "A writes with 33",
                    "sub": "rejected",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Lock service grants a ==monotonically increasing== number",
                "Storage rejects any token **lower** than the highest seen"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. ZooKeeper and etcd",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "ZooKeeper",
                "etcd"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Consensus",
                  "ZAB",
                  "Raft"
                ],
                [
                  "Primitives",
                  "znodes, ephemeral, sequential, watches",
                  "leases, watches, revisions"
                ],
                [
                  "Lock",
                  "lowest sequential ephemeral node",
                  "key on a lease"
                ],
                [
                  "Fencing",
                  "zxid or node version",
                  "revision"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Scope",
              "text": "Both store ==small, critical== data (Kubernetes state, config, election), not bulk storage."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Distributed Coordination Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Distributed Coordination Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Atomic Commit and Sagas",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "2PC",
                "Saga"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Flow",
                  "prepare/vote, then commit/abort",
                  "local transactions + compensations"
                ],
                [
                  "Failure",
                  "{red:blocks} if coordinator dies",
                  "run compensations"
                ],
                [
                  "Consistency",
                  "atomic",
                  "eventual, ==no isolation=="
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:Orchestration}: complex flows needing visibility",
                "{green:Choreography}: few steps, loose coupling"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Reliable Messaging",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Write row + outbox",
                    "sub": "same transaction",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Relay",
                    "sub": "poller or CDC",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Broker",
                    "sub": "at-least-once",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Idempotent consumer",
                    "sub": "dedup",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Outbox== for publishing, ==idempotent consumer== for receiving",
                "Effectively-once = ==at-least-once + dedup=="
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Consensus and Locks",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Majority quorum ==N/2+1==; use **odd** cluster sizes",
                "Raft: ==term== + ==randomized timeout== elects one leader per term"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "ZooKeeper",
                "etcd"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Primitives",
                  "ephemeral + sequential nodes",
                  "leases + revisions"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Locks",
              "text": "Always a ==lease== plus a ==fencing token== checked by the resource. A TTL alone lets a paused holder still write."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "In 2PC, every participant voted YES, then the coordinator crashed before sending any decision. Can a participant safely abort to free its locks?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "No. Its YES was a promise, and others may already have received COMMIT.",
                "It stays in-doubt, holding locks, until the coordinator recovers and replays its logged decision."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A consumer does `send_email(msg)` then `mark_done(msg.id)`. It crashes between the two lines. What happens on redelivery, and what is the fix?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "The email goes out twice, because delivery is at-least-once.",
                "The dedup row can't cover an external call. Pass `msg.id` to the email API as an idempotency key."
              ],
              "example_code": [
                "send_email(msg)",
                "mark_done(msg.id)"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Client A gets lock token 33, then pauses 15s in GC. The lease expires and B gets token 34 and writes. A wakes and writes. What happens?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "With fencing, storage has seen 34 and rejects A's 33.",
                "Without it, A overwrites B's data. The lease alone can't stop that."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
